// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_lnx_disable_ufw.yml
// ID Sigma: 84c9e83c-599a-458a-a0cb-0ecce44e807a
// Título: UFW Disable Attempt
// Descripción: Detects attempts to disable the Uncomplicated Firewall (UFW) on Linux systems.
UFW is a popular firewall management tool that provides an easy-to-use interface for configuring firewall rules.
Disabling UFW can leave a system vulnerable to attacks, as it may allow unauthorized access to network services and resources.

// Fecha de creación: 2023-01-18
// Fecha de modificación: 2026-05-04
// Aplica a: Producto: linux | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: linux
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\linux\process_creation\proc_creation_lnx_disable_ufw.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "/ufw-init" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " force-stop" or ProcessCommandLine contains " stop" or ProcessCommandLine contains " flush")) or (ProcessCommandLine contains "ufw " and ProcessCommandLine contains "disable")
